• longer lead times for shipping;
• language barriers for technical training;
• reduced protection of intellectual property rights in some foreign countries, and related prevalence of generic alternatives to
therapeutics;
• foreign currency exchange rate fluctuations;
• patients’ ability to obtain reimbursement for Viaskin patch products in foreign markets; and
• the interpretation of contractual provisions governed by foreign laws in the event of a contract dispute.
